00:54:33,750 --> 00:54:38,230
you know, anyone who is, you know, can learn by themselves how to code.

903
00:54:38,230 --> 00:54:43,990
and now with AI can probably do that either quicker can be part of the software community.

904
00:54:43,990 --> 00:54:49,109
and the number of people doing development is you know increasing quite significantly.

905
00:54:49,109 --> 00:54:50,870
and I think we lose things between generations.

906
00:54:50,880 --> 00:54:57,430
and we try to remind ourselves that's why architecture I think goes in and out of fashion.

907
00:54:57,430 --> 00:55:01,109
So honestly I I have no idea how architecture will evolve in the future.

908
00:55:01,109 --> 00:55:02,790
but I think we'll still follow the same pattern.

909
00:55:02,790 --> 00:55:04,470
that there will be a period that will go out of fashion again.

910
00:55:04,480 --> 00:55:09,910
and there will be a period that comes back in fashion but hopefully we'll get better.

911
00:55:09,910 --> 00:55:13,910
So rather than going in circles, we'll kind of go in a spiral improving over time.

912
00:55:13,910 --> 00:55:16,230
But I think we'll just go through these phases of it's important,

913
00:55:16,240 --> 00:55:20,150
it's not important, this is what it means, this is not what it means.

914
00:55:20,150 --> 00:55:21,750
But at the end of the day,

915
00:55:21,750 --> 00:55:27,910
I do believe we are building better systems and more systems than in the past.

916
00:55:27,910 --> 00:55:29,910
So I think it's just incremental improvements.

917
00:55:29,920 --> 00:55:35,829
Well, I suppose in a sentence, I hope the future of software architecture is continuous.

918
00:55:35,829 --> 00:55:40,470
There's a relatively few teams I come across have taken this approach up yet.

919
00:55:40,470 --> 00:55:44,790
when it's explained to people often people say yes that makes a lot of sense.

920
00:55:44,790 --> 00:55:51,109
and there's definitely there has been perhaps an unintentional drift towards architecture work being more about technical leadership.

921
00:55:51,109 --> 00:55:55,030
and less about commander control that's very constructive and positive.

922
00:55:55,030 --> 00:56:02,309
I think the core of software architecture is dealing with stakeholders dealing with quality attributes dealing with decisions.

923
00:56:02,309 --> 00:56:04,230
and making trade-offs between them.

924
00:56:04,230 --> 00:56:07,190
and I don't think that has changed from the 1980s.

925
00:56:07,200 --> 00:56:09,910
Well, I suppose software architecture emerged in the 1990s.

926
00:56:09,910 --> 00:56:12,710
I don't think that's changed the 1990s.

927
00:56:12,710 --> 00:56:17,511
You know, we are quite a number of years on from there. So, I don't see that changing.

928
00:56:17,511 --> 00:56:21,190
I see the environment that people need to do.

929
00:56:21,190 --> 00:56:26,150
that in and the technologies they need to do it with perhaps being different.

930
00:56:26,150 --> 00:56:29,750
But I think that fundamental core has been unchanging. So, I don't think that's going to change.

931
00:56:29,760 --> 00:56:31,510
Okay.

932
00:56:31,510 --> 00:56:36,550
And you know sometimes talking about these things is kind of in my head looks like back to. the future.

933
00:56:36,550 --> 00:56:38,069
because there seems to be a lot of things.

934
00:56:38,069 --> 00:56:41,911
that have been you know the core of what we do has been the same for many many. years.

935
00:56:41,920 --> 00:56:47,510
but somehow as Murat said we tend to forget things and then rediscover them again and again.

936
00:56:47,520 --> 00:56:54,390
We do we do yeah but I like the future of architecture is continuous sounds.

937
00:56:54,390 --> 00:56:57,511
and it's like an ad for that could be our slogan. Yeah.

